1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Ernst_I_von_Mansfeld-Vorderort '''Peter Ernst I von Mansfeld-Vorderort'''] - Wikipedia - English (car)
2 CONT * '''born''' - 20 july 1517
2 CONT * '''died''' - 22 May 1604
2 CONT * '''son of''' - Ernst II, van Mansfeld-Vorderort and Dorothea von Solms-Lich
2 CONT * '''married first ''' - Margaretha van Brederode (b.ca.1520 - † 31 May 1554)
2 CONT * '''children''' -
2 CONT # Fredrich 
2 CONT # Karl II, count von Mansfeld zu Friedeburg in Friedeburg, born in Luxembourg 1545, died 14 aug 1596
2 CONT # Polyxene, died after 17 Sept 1591, married Palandes de Nassaau-Chalon 
2 CONT * '''married second''' - Marie de Montmorency († 5 Feb 1570)
2 CONT * '''children''' 
2 CONT # Philipp Oktavian (1564-1591)
2 CONT # Dorothea, married Francisco Verdugo
2 CONT * '''liaison with''' - Anna Benzerath
2 CONT * '''children''' - 
2 CONT # Peter Ernst II von Mansfeld
2 CONT ===Military Career===
2 CONT As a young man Peter Ernst came to the Spanish Netherlands with Charles V.  He participated in the expedition against Tunis in 1535 and became governor of Luxembourg in 1545.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 'Eighty Year's War', he took part in combat under John of Austria, the illegitimate half-brother of King Philip II of Spain and Alexander Farnese, cousin on his mother's side. When Farnese invaded France in 1590, Mansfeld w
2 CONC as appointed Governor ''ad interim'' of the Spanish Netherlands.  When Farnese died in 1592, Von Mansfeld effectively became the governor until Archduke Ernst of Austria took over in 1594
2 CONT ===Knight in the Order of the Golden Fleece===
