1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karl_von_Mansfeld
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl von Mansfeld (1543 – 24 August 1595) was a German general during the Cologne War and the Ottoman-Habsburg wars.
2 CONT
2 CONT Von Mansfeld was the son of Count Peter Ernst I von Mansfeld-Vorderort, born in present day Luxembourg, and was educated in France. He entered the military of Philip II of Spain, and was appointed a general and an admiral in the n
2 CONC avy of the Spanish Netherlands. He was sent to Hungary, where along with Count Mátyás Cseszneky he participated in the siege of Esztergom in 1595 during the Long War. He died shortly thereafter, probably of his wounds, in Komárom.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT He married twice, first to Diane de Cossé and, second, to Marie Christine von Egmond, who died 1622.
2 CONT
2 CONT She had, from her second marriage, a son, Alexandre de Bournonville Duc de Bournonville, Comte de Henin-Lietard (14 September 1585, Brussels, died 21 March 1656), and, probably with Mansfeld, a second son, Antoine III de Lalaing (
2 CONC born between 1588 and 1590 and died 26 September 1613), Count of Hoogstraeten, who married Maria Margaretha de Berlaymont, daughter of Claude Berlaymont, also known as Haultpenne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings
2 CONT
2 CONT From his father's first marriage on 1.4.1542 to Margaretha van Brederode (*ca 1520, died 31 may 1554);
2 CONT
2 CONT  Friedrich, *1542, died 1559
2 CONT
2 CONT  Polyxene, +after 17 September 1591; m. Palamedes von Nassau-Chalon (+1600)
2 CONT
2 CONT Step Siblings:
2 CONT
2 CONT From his father's second marriage 22.2.1562 Marie de Montmorency (+5.2.1570)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Philipp Oktavian, *1564, +1591
2 CONT
2 CONT  Dorothea; m. Franz Verdugo
2 CONT
2 CONT Natural Sibling [by Anna von Benzerath]
2 CONT
2 CONT  Peter Ernst II von Mansfeld *1580,  † near Sarajevo 29.11.1626
