1 OCCU Graf von Schleiden
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Ernst von der Marck, Graf von Schleiden=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Philipp von der Marck‑ Baron Lumen and Katharina von Manderscheid-Schleiden
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married= 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Married  (1) Sibylle (Sybille) Gräfin von Hohenzollern‑Hechingen.''' They married after 25 May 1615.
2 CONT * '''Married (2) Anna Margareta von Manderscheid‑Blankenheim''' (sometimes spelled Manderscheid‑Blankenberg). They married on 14 November 1623. This marriage is documented in noble‑line compendia, though the children from this uni
2 CONC on are less prominently listed than Franz Anton from the first marriage. 
2 CONT * '''Married (3) Katharina Reicherts''' was his third wife, with the marriage taking place around 1620–1645.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ernst’s only clearly documented child from these two marriages is Franz Anton, born from his union with Sibylle von Hohenzollern‑Hechingen; the second marriage to Anna Margareta von Manderscheid‑Blankenheim is recorded but with
2 CONC out strong evidence of surviving children.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Sibylle (Sybille) Gräfin von Hohenzollern‑Hechingen=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From this marriage he had at least one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Franz Anton, Graf von der Marck''' (also called Franz Anton von der Marck‑Schleiden), who succeeded him in the Schleiden line and is recorded as a son of Ernst and Sibylle in multiple genealogical sources
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
