1 NAME Wolfgang /von Oettingen-Wallerstein/
2 GIVN Wolfgang
2 SURN von Oettingen-Wallerstein
2 _MARNM von Oettingen-Wallerstein
1 NAME Wolfgang III, Graf von Oettingen zu Wallerstein
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 26 MAY 1573
1 DEAT
2 DATE 7 MAY 1598
2 ADDR
3 CITY Vienna
3 STAE Vienna
3 CTRY Austria
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00109873&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Wolfgang was born in Wallerstein on 26 May 1573, the son of Wilhelm II, Graf von Oettingen-Wallerstein, and Johanna, Gräfin von Hohenzollern-Sigmaringen. His marriage was caught in controversy over the suitability of his
2 CONC  bride. About 1595 he married Johanna de Mol, daughter of Pierre de Mol, Heer van Hooghvorst, and Levina Borluut. In order to gain his father's consent to his marriage, in 1594 Wolfgang had to sign a charter for his successors ren
2 CONC ouncing all their succession rights to the countship, though he himself was freed from this stricture. Subsequent researches established that Johanna came from a presentable knightly family in Brabant, from which the Barons of Her
2 CONC ent originated. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wolfgang and Johanna had a son Ernst II who would have progeny, and three daughters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wolfgang died on 7 September 1598, four years before his father and 15 years before his wife. His son Ernst II succeeded his father in Wallerstein.
