1 NAME Ernest Casimir Casimir /von Nassau-Weilburg/
2 GIVN Ernest Casimir Casimir
2 SURN von Nassau-Weilburg
2 _MARNM von Nassau-Weilburg
2 NICK Ernst Casimir
1 NAME Ernest Casimir, Count of Nassau-Weilburg
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 STAE Hessen
3 CTRY Deutschland(HRR)
1 BIRT
2 DATE 15 NOV 1607
2 ADDR
3 CITY Saarbrücken
3 STAE Saarland
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE 16 APR 1655
2 ADDR
3 CITY Weilburg
3 STAE Hesse
3 CTRY Germany
1 TITL Graf
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ernest_Casimir,_Count_of_Nassau-Weilburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Ernest Casimir of Nassau-Weilburg (15 November 1607 – April 1655) was the founder the younger line of Nassau-Weilburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a son of Louis II, Count of Nassau-Weilburg and his wife Anna Maria of Hesse-Kassel (1567–1626).
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Saarbrücken.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father, Louis II, had been able to unite all the territories of Walram branch of Nassau. After his death in 1621, the territories were divided among four brothers, with William Louis, the olderst, acting as regent for the youn
2 CONC gest two. When Otto, the youngest died in 1632, and Ernest Casimir came of age, the tree surviving brothers divided the territory anew. The oldest, William Louis, received Nassau-Saarbrücken, John received Idstein and Ernest Casim
2 CONC ir received Weilburg, Merenberg, Gleiberg, Hüttenberg, Reichelsheim, Kirchheim, Stauf, Bolanden and parts of Homburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ernest Casimir did not spend much time in his own territory. In 1634, he had to flee from the Thirty Years' War. He fled to Metz and returned after the 1648 Peace of Westphalia. Even after the peace had been signed, it took a whil
2 CONC e before all rightful rulers had been restored to power.
2 CONT
2 CONT During this period, the brothers concluded the Treaty of Gotha of 16 July 1651, in which division of 1632 was confirmed and again adjusted.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in Weilburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1634 Ernest Casimir married Anna Maria of Sayn-Wittgenstein-Hachenburg (1610–1656). She was the daughter of Count William II of Sayn-Wittgenstein-Hachenburg (1569–1623). The couple had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT  William Louis (1634–1636)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Marie Eleonore (1636–1678), married Count Casimir of Eberstein (d. 1660)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Casimir (1638–1639)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Frederick (1640–1675), married Christiane Elisabeth of Sayn-Wittgenstein-Homburg (1646–1678), daughter of Count Ernest of Sayn-Wittgenstein-Homburg (1599–1649)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
