1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Links:==
2 CONT *[http://www.geneall.net/D/per_page.php?id=337053 Geneall]
2 CONT *[http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georg_Friedrich_(Waldeck-Eisenberg)_ Wikipedia Deutsch]
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_Georg_Friedrich_of_Waldeck
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Georg Friedrich of Waldeck (31 January 1620, Arolsen – 19 November 1692, Arolsen) was a German and Dutch Field Marshal .
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1641, Waldeck entered the service of the States-General of the Netherlands; later in 1651, in the service of Brandenburg, he reached the highest rank as minister. He changed the foreign policy completely by abandoning the allia
2 CONC nce with the Emperor and trying to forge a coalition with the Protestant princes.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1656 he arranged a coalition with Sweden, and commanded the cavalry in the Battle of Warsaw (1656) against Poland. He was dismissed in 1658 when Frederick William, Elector of Brandenburg made peace with Poland.
2 CONT
2 CONT After that he fought under Charles X Gustav of Sweden against Denmark, as German Reichsfeldmarschall in 1664 near Sankt Gotthard. In 1683 he commanded Bavarian troops during the Battle of Vienna. In 1685 he fought as a free-lancer
2 CONC  for the Duke of Lorraine and the Elector of Bavaria.
2 CONT
2 CONT After William III left for England in 1688 to claim the English throne, Waldeck was appointed Field Marshal of William's forces during the War of the Grand Alliance in the Spanish Netherlands. Although he was victorious at the Bat
2 CONC tle of Walcourt in 1689, the following year he suffered a heavy defeat at the hands of Marshal Luxembourg at the Battle of Fleurus.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1691, he was again outmanoeuvred by Luxembourg and defeated at the Battle of Leuze. After this defeat Waldeck was appointed chief-of-staff of the Dutch States Army. He died on 19 November 1692 in Arolsen.
