1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Countess Johanna of Hanau-Münzenberg (1610 – 13 September 1673) was a daughter of Count Albert of Hanau-Münzenberg-Schwarzenfels and Countess Ehrengard of Isenburg (1577 – 1637). Hanau-Münzenberg-Schwarzenfels was 
2 CONC a cadet branch of Hanau-Münzenberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johanna of Hanau-Münzenberg married twice:
2 CONT
2 CONT From September 1637[1] with Wild- and Rhinegrave Wolfgang Friedrich of Salm (1589 – 24 December 1638). The marriage did not produce offspring.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 14 December 1646 with Prince Manuel António of Portugal (1600 – 1666), a Dutch-Portuguese nobleman with family relationship to the House of Orange-Nassau. Their relation produced the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilhelmina Amalia (1647 – 14 November 1647).
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth Maria (20 November 1648 in Delft – 15 October 1717 in Vianen), married on 11 April 1678 with Lieutenant colonel Baron Adriaan of Gent (16 Februar 1645 in The Hague – 10 August 1708).
2 CONT
2 CONT The sources point out that the countess brought in little to the marriage.[2] Due to the Thirty Years' War, the lineage Hanau-Münzenberg-Schwarzenfels had become impoverished. Seemingly in 1633, the family had to escape from the B
2 CONC urg Schwarzenfels, first to Worms and later to Strasbourg where they struggled with financial problems. This explains her relatively advanced age for the first marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT in, http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johanna_of_Hanau-M%C3%BCnzenberg
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Johanna Von Salm-Dhaun (nascida Condessa Von Hanau-Münzenberg n.12 de abr de 1610,  Müzenberg. Casamento com: D. Manuel de Portugal, 11 de jul de 1646,   Haia, Holanda, Morte: 26 de jul de 1673,  Bruxelas, Bélgica.
2 CONT
2 CONT Filha que segue:  D. Isabel Maria Emília De Portugal (Baronesa De Ghent ) n. 20 de nov de 1648--15 de out de 1717
2 CONT
2 CONT Casamento com: Adrian, Barão de Ghent, 11 de abr de 1678 11 de abr de 1678
2 CONT
2 CONT
