1 OCCU Queen of Prussia, Queen Consort in Prussia, , Princess of Hanover, Sophie Charlotte Hanover, Princess of Hanover (nn mrg), Herzogin von Braunschweig und Lüneburg ( Königin  in PREUSSEN (1701 - 1705), Kurfürstin von Brandenburg (16
2 CONC 88-1705)
1 TITL Queen
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sophia Charlotte of Hanover (30 October 1668, at Schloss Iburg in Bad Iburg near Osnabrück – 1 February 1705 in Hanover) was the daughter of Ernst August, Elector of Hanover and Sophia of the Palatinate. Her eldest
2 CONC  brother Georg Ludwig would succeed to the British throne in 1714 as King George I. She was once rumoured to be marrying the widower Louis XIV. By marrying Frederick I of Prussia, she became Queen in Prussia. Their only child to r
2 CONC each maturity became Frederick William I of Prussia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophia Charlotte is mainly remembered for her friendship and correspondence with her mother's good friend and tutor Gottfried Leibniz, whose avowed disciple she became. Sophia Charlotte's death of pneumonia on 21 January 1705 (OS;
2 CONC  1 February NS), when she was 36 years of age, devastated him.
2 CONT
