1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.remy-corporation.com/genealogie/gencarte/robert_thompson4a6.html
2 CONT
2 CONT JACOB6 REMY, JR. (JACQUES (JACOB)5, PIERRE4, JACQUES3, GEORGE2, DIDIER1) was born 1675 in Westmoreland Co., Virginia, USA, and died 1726 in Westmoreland Co., Virginia, USA. He married ANN SANFORD Abt. 1695, daughter of ROBERT SANF
2 CONC ORD and ANN UNKNOWN. She was born Abt. 1675.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of JACOB REMY and ANN SANFORD are:
2 CONT
2 CONT i. JOHN7 REMY, b. Abt. 1696.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. WILLIAM REMY, b. Abt. 1698.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will
2 CONT
2 CONT 1654-1800 Westmoreland County, Virginia Wills [Augusta B. Fothergill];
2 CONT REMY, JACOB, 23 Feb. 1726; 31 May 1727.
2 CONT Sons John, Jacob, William, Benjamin and Joseph my land ; my wife ; my decd. father.
2 CONT ===
2 CONT * 1723-1726 Westmoreland County, Virginia Deeds & Will Book 8, Part 1 [Antient Press]; Page 85
2 CONT * IN THE NAME OF GOD. Amen. I JACOB REMY of Westmoreland County and of Copely Parish being in perfect mind and memory tho weake in body, do make this my Last Will and Testament in manner and form following, yt. is to say, „-
2 CONT * Imprimis. I commend my Soyle which is my immortal! part into ye hands of mighty God my Creator haveing a lively faith in Xt. Christ yt: all my sins shall bee forgiven me, my body I commit to ye Earth from whence it came, yt: it 
2 CONC to receive a decent burial according to ye discretion of my Loving Wife and my loving Son, JOHN, whom appoint Executrix and Executor of this my Last Will and Testament, And as touching my worldly goods and Estate with wch, it hath
2 CONC  pleased God to bless me with, I give and beqeuath as followeth;
2 CONT * Imprimis, I give and bequeath unto my loving Son, JOHN, all my working tools and my Halbard,
2 CONT * Item. I give unto my loving Son, JACOB, and his male heir two hundred and thirty acres of land, one hundred and seven acres being the land formerly my Fathers, and thirty acres I bout of EDWARD RANSDELL, with ninety three acres 
2 CONC I bought of RICHARD SUTTON with the Hand Mill. Now in case ye said JACOB die without male heir yt. yn, it is Inv Will yt ye said Land returne to my Son, BENJAMIN, and his male heire and for want of such male heire of his to return
2 CONC e unto my Son, JOSEPH;
2 CONT * Item. I give and bequeath unto my loveing Sone, WILLIAM, my walking Cane;
2 CONT * Item. It is my Will and desire yt: after ye decease of my said Wife, yt: all my personable Estate as it shall be found shall equally be devided amongst all my Children. It is further my Will and desire yt: my loving Wife noways 
2 CONC be molested or disturbed on ye said Land and Plantation she now is on dureing her natural! life. I doe hereby revoke all former Wills desireing this to be my Last. In Wittness whereof I have hereunto set my hand and seal this twen
2 CONC ty thrid day of February 1726/7
2 CONT * Signed Sealed and declared to bee his Last Will
2 CONT * and Testament in the presents of us
2 CONT * ABRM. VELDEN, JACOB REMY
2 CONT * WILLIAM SANFORD, RICHD: SUTTON
2 CONT * Westmoreld. ss. At a Court held for the sd. County the 31st day of May 1727
2 CONT * This Last, Will and Testament of JACOB REMY, deced., was presented into Court by his Relict and JOHN REMEY, the Executors therein named, who made Oath thereto and being proved by the Oaths of WILLIAM SANFORD and RICHARD SUTTON, 
2 CONC two of the witnesses thereto, is admitted to Record . Test G. TURBERVILE, Cl Co W.
2 CONT * Recorded the Sixth day of June 1727 pr. G, T. C. C. W
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Will of Jacob Remy, dated July 1702, proved Dec. 5, 1721;
2 CONT * To loving wife Mary, the furniture in her room.
2 CONT * To oldest son William, one shilling on demand.
2 CONT * To youngest son Jacob, 200 acres of land, the land on which I now live.
2 CONT * Westmoreland Co., Va., Will Book 7, p.254.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
