1 NAME Marie-Gabrielle /de Lalaing/ 9° comtesse de Hoogstraeten
2 GIVN Marie-Gabrielle
2 SURN de Lalaing
2 NSFX 9° comtesse de Hoogstraeten
2 NICK Marie Gabriele Comtesse de Lalaing
2 NICK Comtesse de Hoogstraeten
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 14 DEC 1638
2 ADDR
3 CITY Maastricht
3 STAE Limburg
3 CTRY Netherlands
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 FEB 1709
2 ADDR
3 CITY Antwerpen
3 STAE Vlaanderen
3 CTRY Belgium
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Note's
2 CONT Marie Gabrielle von Lalain (de Lalaing), 9th Countess of Hoogstraten * around December 14, 1639 in Maastricht, † February 8, 1709 in Antwerp
2 CONT - from 1691 to 1709 9th Countess of Hoogstraten and Hornes
2 CONT - Baroness von Leuze, as her father's heir
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage on December 14, 1657 in Gravenhage (The Hague) to Karl Florentin zu Salm, Wildgraf and Rheingraf zu Dhaun-Neufville * 01/14/1638, killed in Petershem near Maastrich 09/04/1676
2 CONT
2 CONT For Hoogstraten, the heiress of the county, Marie de Lalaing, had established the male primogeniture in her will (HA Hoogstraeten Urknr.22).
2 CONT _____
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marie-Gabrielle de Lalaing''' + 1709 
2 CONT - 9° countess of Hoogstraeten (1691, after her brother) last of the name, 
2 CONT - baroness of Leuze, Eyne and Pecques, 
2 CONT - lady of Eeckeren, Hoeven and Capellen
2 CONT
2 CONT married Charles-Florentin, 
2 CONT - Wild & Reingraf de Salm (Rhingrave zu Salm) in Neufviller, Daun and Kirbourg,
2 CONT - count of Salm, 
2 CONT - baron of Tournebu, 
2 CONT - lord of Neufville(r), 
2 CONT - General-Governor of Breda
2 CONT - stem of the Princes of Salm-Salm & dukes of Hoogstraeten
2 CONT [erection in duchy by Charles VI in 1740] (Nicolas Léopold de Salm inherits
2 CONT of François Paul de Lalaing )
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Pattou, Etienne, Famille & Seigneurs de Lalaing, Racines et Histoire''
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''Marie-Gabrielle de Lalaing''', countess of Hoochstrate and Homes, after her brother, married to Charles, count DE SALM, of the house Wild and Rhine Graff. Of which posterity, with erection of Hooogstraet in duchy, the year 1740
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Brassart, Felix, Société Académique, editor. Souvenirs De La Flandre Wallonne, Catalogue des Nobels de Nom, de Lalaing, Dix-Septieme, L. Crépin, 1882. un Comite Historique et Archeologique: Memories of Walloon Flanders: pp. 89.'
2 CONC '
