1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Johann Christian II. De Solms-Baruth was born 29 June 1733 in Baruth, Germany to Johann Karl De Solms-Baruth (1702-1735) and Henriette L.W. zur Lippe-Biesterfeld (1711-1752) and died 7 October 1800 in Klitschdorf o
2 CONC f unspecified causes. 
2 CONT * He married Wilhelmine Luise zur Lippe-Biesterfeld (1733-1766) 30 January 1764 in Wehrau. 
2 CONT * He married Friederike Reuss zu Köstritz (1748-1798) 10 March 1767 in Berlin. 
2 CONT * Notable ancestors include Alfred the Great (849-899), Charlemagne (747-814), Hugh Capet (c940-996), William I of England (1027-1087), Rurik (c832-879), Henry II of England (1133-1189). Ancestors are from Germany, the Netherlands
2 CONC , France, Byzantium, the United Kingdom, Russia, Belgium, Spain, Belarus, Hungary, Italy, the Czech Republic, Switzerland, Austria, Bohemia, Denmark, Poland, Lithuania.
2 CONT
